    * - `"skipBom": false or true`
    *   - If true, if the input starts with the Unicode byte order mark (BOM),
    *     it is skipped.
+   * - `"strictNumbers": false or true`
+   *   - If true, numbers must match the RFC 8259 grammar exactly. Leading
+   *     zeros (`01`), a leading `+`, a trailing decimal point (`1.`), and an
+   *     empty exponent (`1e`) are rejected. Defaults to false for
+   *     compatibility with lenient jsoncpp inputs.
    *
    * You can examine `settings_` yourself to see the defaults. You can also
    * write and read them just like any JSON Value.
